WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.200
U.S. strikes on Iran's Keshe Miland raised the risk of higher energy costs for households worldwide. This is Omni View, episode 225. Lebanon's electricity cuts, Hong Kong land search rules, and Mogadishu talks come next, then understanding the issue. U.S. officials described the Keshe Miland operation as limited and defensive, according to the British Broadcasting Corporation, or BBC. The action took place one day before U.S. midterm elections.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.520
politicians, the nationwide congressional vote.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.480
It records that the attacks followed earlier signals from both U.S. and Iranian leaders

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.580
that diplomatic channels remained open.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.960
The U.S. and Iranian presidents had indicated a willingness to explore diplomatic solutions

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.900
the previous day.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.060
Oil prices rose on the news, according to separate market reporting.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.680
Traders assessed whether the limited scope would contain any impact on supply.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.060
CNBC reports on the same operation through the immediate market effects rather than the

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.678
diplomatic sequence. Officials kept using the words limited and defensive, even as those

00:01:03.678 --> 00:01:09.238
prices moved. The previous day's talk of exploring solutions did not prevent the use of force

00:01:09.238 --> 00:01:14.098
the next day. What remains on the record is that both governments had still been signaling

00:01:14.098 --> 00:01:20.481
that channels for talk were not closed. Lebanon's energy ministry began shutting off power to roughly

00:01:20.481 --> 00:01:26.121
100 public bodies that owe unpaid bills. The move follows months of disputes between the

00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:30.101
energy minister and the cabinet over fuel costs and supply shortfalls.

00:01:30.621 --> 00:01:35.461
State electricity in Beirut now runs for only two to four hours a day in many areas.

00:01:36.121 --> 00:01:40.241
Al Jazeera reporting highlights how political disagreements and the effects of regional

00:01:40.241 --> 00:01:43.761
conflict have worsened an already fragile electricity system.

00:01:44.301 --> 00:01:49.341
That short state supply has forced households and offices onto costly private generators.

00:01:50.331 --> 00:01:54.781
Experts cited in the same coverage point to long-standing corruption across the supply chain

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.041
as the core obstacle to lasting fixes.

00:01:57.661 --> 00:02:03.441
The World Bank, the International Development Lender, projects 17.5 percent year-on-year

00:02:03.441 --> 00:02:05.141
inflation for Lebanon this year.

00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:09.881
Fuel costs for those private generators have been rising sharply because of the regional

00:02:09.881 --> 00:02:10.421
conflict.

00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:15.641
Analysts quoted in that reporting say the sector needs deep structural reform rather than

00:02:15.641 --> 00:02:16.561
temporary measures.

00:02:17.161 --> 00:02:21.781
They argue corruption reaches every stage from the purchase of fuel through to distribution.

00:02:21.781 --> 00:02:26.101
The ministry's cutoff of indebted public bodies is the immediate lever.

00:02:26.741 --> 00:02:30.381
The unpaid bills sit on top of that longer fight over fuel and supply.

00:02:31.407 --> 00:02:35.687
Journalists in Hong Kong who are denied access to land records will have to seek judicial

00:02:35.687 --> 00:02:38.167
review, a court test of the refusal.

00:02:38.887 --> 00:02:43.007
Officials told lawmakers that the government will process approved requests within one or

00:02:43.007 --> 00:02:46.127
two working days, the South China Morning Post reports.

00:02:46.847 --> 00:02:50.827
The change sits inside a review of eight pieces of subsidiary legislation.

00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:53.567
The detailed rules that govern land searches.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:58.687
Lawmakers asked whether the new rules could limit media scrutiny of property transactions.

00:02:59.447 --> 00:03:03.447
Officials answered by stressing faster routine delivery for legitimate applicants.

00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:09.367
The legislative council, Hong Kong's lawmaking body, had a subcommittee hold its first meeting

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.227
on the proposed arrangement on the day that pledge was made.

00:03:12.887 --> 00:03:17.567
Those lawmakers worry is that a refusal would push reporters toward court proceedings instead

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.347
of ordinary administrative channels.

00:03:19.347 --> 00:03:24.747
The government's answer is speed for people it treats as legitimate, not an open counter

00:03:24.747 --> 00:03:26.027
to the scrutiny concern.

00:03:26.347 --> 00:03:30.947
A refused journalist would still need a judge, even if an approved search is promised in

00:03:30.947 --> 00:03:31.567
a day or two.

00:03:32.468 --> 00:03:37.228
Closer cooperation between two neighbors was the agenda when Somalia's permanent secretary

00:03:37.228 --> 00:03:40.948
for foreign affairs, a senior diplomat met Kenya's ambassador.

00:03:41.648 --> 00:03:43.448
The meeting took place in Mogadishu.

00:03:43.928 --> 00:03:49.008
All Africa reporting, drawing on Shebel, frames the encounter as a routine diplomatic step

00:03:49.008 --> 00:03:54.880
between the two countries. The discussion was about ways to strengthen ties. Switzerland's

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:01.080
consumer price index, the official measure of living costs, rose 1.5% year-on-year in October,

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:08.520
above the 1.3% forecast. The Swiss franc reached a 7-week high against the dollar, TMGM reports,

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:14.100
and energy prices were the main driver of the stronger reading. The monthly figure came in at

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.620
0.2 percent instead of the flat reading markets had expected.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:22.380
Coverage links the Franks moved to that data release and to uncertainty ahead of those

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.960
same U.S. midterm elections.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.500
The Swiss National Bank, the country's central bank, may face earlier consideration of

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.960
rate hikes if energy-driven inflation persists.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.040
ING strategists quoted in the reporting say they do not expect the midterm results

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.820
to cause structural shifts in foreign exchange markets.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:47.740
They add that a democratic sweep of both chambers could increase pressure on the dollar through fears of tighter regulation on technology stocks.

00:04:48.704 --> 00:04:55.604
Apple stock declined after the company reported earnings that disappointed investors on future margins, CNBC reports.

00:04:56.424 --> 00:04:59.224
Palantir shares also dropped sharply on the same day.

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:03.244
The moves are attributed to investor reaction to the earnings releases.

00:05:04.314 --> 00:05:09.634
Kenya's latest national survey is progress worth knowing on teenage pregnancy among older teens.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:15.314
The Kenya National Bureau of Statistics, the government statistics agency, found that

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:21.134
the share of girls aged 15 to 19 who have ever been pregnant fell to 11.9%.

00:05:21.134 --> 00:05:24.794
That compares with 14.8% in 2022.

00:05:25.654 --> 00:05:30.414
All Africa, citing Capitol FM, presents the decline as measured across the country.

00:05:31.361 --> 00:05:35.661
Across the rest of the day's notes, Hong Kong homeowners prompted a government rethink

00:05:35.661 --> 00:05:41.241
of proxy vote proposals, after public resistance led officials to study alternatives on a state

00:05:41.241 --> 00:05:47.541
management rules, according to the South China Morning Post. All 23 children hospitalized in

00:05:47.541 --> 00:05:53.341
Uganda's Boutable District after a drug mix-up are now out of danger and expected to be discharged.

00:05:54.181 --> 00:05:59.541
Air India's chief executive said the airline is seeking more wide-body jets and sees profitability

00:05:59.541 --> 00:06:06.381
soon, Reuters reports. An advisor to a European Union or EU court said Google's use of press

00:06:06.381 --> 00:06:12.901
content by an artificial intelligence, or AI chatbot, may breach copyright rules. To

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:18.041
really understand how targeted force shows up in oil prices, start with how futures traders

00:06:18.041 --> 00:06:23.541
treat duration and scale, not the mere fact that force was used. A common reading treats

00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:28.481
any military action that touches a major oil producer as an automatic trigger for a lasting

00:06:28.481 --> 00:06:29.181
price spike.

00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:34.601
Markets in practice separate strikes that threaten sustained cuts and supply from operations

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:37.561
that officials explicitly label limited and defensive.

00:06:38.381 --> 00:06:41.561
Traders are pricing the expected length and size of a disruption.

00:06:42.241 --> 00:06:44.621
They are not pricing the headline that force occurred.

00:06:45.281 --> 00:06:50.661
When public statements leave diplomatic channels open, futures often print only a brief spike.

00:06:51.141 --> 00:06:55.381
That pattern differs from the multi-week rallies that have followed larger interruptions.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:07:01.081
The useful distinction is between an actual supply shock and a short-term risk premium that

00:07:01.081 --> 00:07:03.441
can fade once the limited nature is confirmed.

00:07:03.981 --> 00:07:09.141
The same lens helps on currencies, a frank rally that looks like fear can be a direct response

00:07:09.141 --> 00:07:12.841
to a domestic inflation print rather than a broad flight from risk.

00:07:13.723 --> 00:07:17.803
Cross-check official statements against data from more than one region before treating

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:19.103
a story as escalation.

00:07:19.663 --> 00:07:24.123
Government releases and market data prints are clearer signals than secondhand commentary.

00:07:24.123 --> 00:07:28.363
accounts from outlets based in different countries show which facts are shared

00:07:28.363 --> 00:07:32.976
and where the interpretation splits. The next time a headline says oil is

00:07:32.976 --> 00:07:36.996
surging on Middle East strikes, look for whether the piece names the size of the

00:07:36.996 --> 00:07:41.956
facilities hit and how long any disruption is expected to last. BBC coverage

00:07:41.956 --> 00:07:46.836
lingers on the limited defensive label and on diplomacy still being described as

00:07:46.836 --> 00:07:52.696
open, while CNBC treats the same episode chiefly as a market event. US midterm

00:07:52.696 --> 00:07:56.656
From results, we'll test whether foreign exchange desks see only passing dollar noise

00:07:57.076 --> 00:08:01.896
as ING expects or a sharper regulatory scare if Democrats take both chambers.

00:08:02.416 --> 00:08:04.136
That wraps up today's OmniView.

00:08:04.736 --> 00:08:09.296
Remember, the best informed people read more than one perspective, and the calmest ones

00:08:09.296 --> 00:08:12.676
know that most days, somewhere, something is quietly getting better.

